# A Desktop window's size (DesktopSizing, option 2): the window adapts to the other Mac's Desktop, never the
# other way. The synthetic host's Desktop is its 1512 × 949-point test pattern, streamed by the test host's software encoder at 1x (1512 × 948, even sides): taken as 1x points (DesktopSizing.points).
# A new Desktop window opens at Actual Size (or fitted to this Mac's screen); Keep the Desktop's Shape keeps its
# picture area at the frame's proportions; off, a window can take any size (bars, as before); Fit to Screen and
# the green button give the largest window of that shape.
wait apps 30
view keep on
# The launcher's Keep Desktop shape switch, the settings' last row.
click 180 591
expect keepDesktopShape == false
click 180 591
expect keepDesktopShape == true
click 75 242
wait stream 15
wait desktopshape 15
expect streamWindows.0.desktop == true
expect streamWindows.0.frameSize == 1512x948
expect streamWindows.0.points == 1512x948
expect streamWindows.0.keptShape == true
expect streamWindows.0.actualSize == true
view keep off
expect keepDesktopShape == false
view size 900 400
expect streamWindows.0.content == 900x400
expect streamWindows.0.keptShape == false
view keep on
expect keepDesktopShape == true
expect streamWindows.0.keptShape == true
view size 900 400
view fit
expect streamWindows.0.keptShape == true
expect streamWindows.0.fitsScreen == true
view size 700 500
view zoom
expect streamWindows.0.fitsScreen == true
view actual
expect streamWindows.0.actualSize == true
snap desktopsize-actual.png all
